DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ccaacchheessttaatt(())  queries  the  number  of  cached pages, dirty pages, pages
       marked for writeback, evicted pages, and recently evicted pages in  the
       byte range specified by _._o_f_f and _._l_e_n in the ccaacchheessttaatt__rraannggee structure.

       An  evicted  page  is one that was previously in the page cache but has
       since been evicted.  A page is considered recently evicted if its reen‐
       try into the cache would indicate active usage under memory pressure.

       The results are returned in a ccaacchheessttaatt structure, pointed  to  by  the
       _c_s_t_a_t argument.

       The  _._o_f_f  and  _._l_e_n  fields  must  be  non‐negative.  If _._l_e_n _> _0, the
       queried range is [_._o_f_f, _._o_f_f_+_._l_e_n].  If _l_e_n _=_= _0,  the  range  is  from
       _._o_f_f to the end of the file.

       The _f_l_a_g_s argument is reserved for future use and must be set to 00.

       Currently, hhuuggeettllbbffss files are not supported.

